"which provides `io.quarkus.test.kafka.KafkaCompanionResource` - an "
"implementation of `io.quarkus.test.common."
"QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then use `@QuarkusTestResource` to configure the Kafka Companion in tests, "
"for example:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@InjectKafkaCompanion` injects the `KafkaCompanion` instance, configured to "
"access the Kafka broker created for tests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `KafkaCompanion` to create producer task which writes 10 records to "
"'orders' topic."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create consumer task which subscribes to 'orders-processed' topic and "
"consumes 10 records."
msgstr ""

msgid "Await completion of the consumer task."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the Kafka Dev Service is available during tests, `KafkaCompanionResource` "
"uses the created Kafka broker, otherwise it creates a Kafka broker using "
"https://github.com/strimzi/test-container[Strimzi Test Container]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The configuration of the created Kafka broker can be customized using "
"`@ResourceArg`, for example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom test resource"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can start a Kafka broker in a test resource.\n"
"The following snippet shows a test resource starting a Kafka broker using "
"https://www.testcontainers.org/modules/kafka/[Testcontainers]:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configure the Kafka bootstrap location, so the application connects to this "
"broker."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Services for Kafka"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If any Kafka-related extension is present (e.g. `quarkus-smallrye-reactive-"
"messaging-kafka`), Dev Services for Kafka automatically starts a Kafka "
"broker in dev mode and when running tests.\n"
"So, you don't have to start a broker manually.\n"
"The application is configured automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling / Disabling Dev Services for Kafka"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Services for Kafka is automatically enabled unless:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.kafka.devservices.enabled` is set to `false`"
msgstr ""

msgid "the `kafka.bootstrap.servers` is configured"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"all the Reactive Messaging Kafka channels have the `bootstrap.servers` "
"attribute set"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Kafka relies on Docker to start the broker.\n"
"If your environment does not support Docker, you will need to start the "
"broker manually, or connect to an already running broker.\n"
"You can configure the broker address using `kafka.bootstrap.servers`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared broker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most of the time you need to share the broker between applications.\n"
"Dev Services for Kafka implements a _service discovery_ mechanism for your "
"multiple Quarkus applications running in _dev_ mode to share a single broker."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need multiple (shared) brokers, you can configure the `quarkus.kafka."
"devservices.service-name` attribute and indicate the broker name.\n"
"It looks for a container with the same value, or starts a new one if none "
"can be found.\n"
"The default service name is `kafka`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sharing is enabled by default in dev mode, but disabled in test mode.\n"
"You can disable the sharing with `quarkus.kafka.devservices.shared=false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting the port"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Dev Services for Kafka picks a random port and configures the "
"application.\n"
"You can set the port by configuring the `quarkus.kafka.devservices.port` "
"property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that the Kafka advertised address is automatically configured with the "
"chosen port."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuring the image"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Kafka supports https://redpanda.com[Redpanda] and https://"
"strimzi.io[Strimzi] (in https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/config/"
"kraft/README.md[Kraft] mode)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Redpanda is a Kafka compatible event streaming platform.\n"
"Because it provides a faster startup time dev services defaults to "
"`vectorized/redpanda` images.\n"
"You can select any version from https://hub.docker.com/r/vectorized/redpanda."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Strimzi provides container images and Operators for running Apache Kafka on "
"Kubernetes.\n"
"While Strimzi is optimized for Kubernetes, the images work perfectly in "
"classic container environments.\n"
"Strimzi container images run \"genuine\" Kafka broker on JVM, which is "
"slower to start."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For Strimzi, you can select any image with a Kafka version which has Kraft "
"support (2.8.1 and higher) from https://quay.io/repository/strimzi-test-"
"container/test-container?tab=tags"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuring Kafka topics"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can configure the Dev Services for Kafka to create topics once the "
"broker is started.\n"
"Topics are created with given number of partitions and 1 replica."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The following example creates a topic named `test` with 3 partitions, and a "
"second topic named `messages` with 2 partitions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a topic already exists with the given name, the creation is skipped,\n"
"without trying to re-partition the existing topic to a different number of "
"partitions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can configure timeout for Kafka admin client calls used in topic "
"creation using `quarkus.kafka.devservices.topic-partitions-timeout`, it "
"defaults to 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Transactional and Idempotent producers support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the Red Panda broker is configured to enable transactions and "
"idempotence features.\n"
"You can disable those using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes Service Bindings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Kafka extension supports\n"
"xref:deploying-to-kubernetes.adoc[Service Binding Specification for "
"Kubernetes].\n"
"You can enable this by adding the `quarkus-kubernetes-service-binding` "
"extension to your application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When running in appropriately configured Kubernetes clusters, Kafka "
"extension will pull its Kafka broker connection configuration from the "
"service binding available inside the cluster, without the need for user "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "Execution model"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reactive Messaging invokes user's methods on an I/O thread.\n"
"Thus, by default, the methods must not block.\n"
"As described in <<blocking-processing>>, you need to add the `@Blocking` "
"annotation on the method if this method will block the caller thread."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See the xref:quarkus-reactive-architecture.adoc[Quarkus Reactive "
"Architecture documentation] for further details on this topic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Channel Decorators"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SmallRye Reactive Messaging supports decorating incoming and outgoing "
"channels for implementing cross-cutting concerns such as monitoring, tracing "
"or message interception. For more information on implementing decorators and "
"message interceptors see the http://smallrye.io/smallrye-reactive-messaging/"
"3.19.1/concepts/decorators/[SmallRye Reactive Messaging documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration Reference"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More details about the SmallRye Reactive Messaging configuration can be "
"found in the https://smallrye.io/smallrye-reactive-messaging/latest/kafka/"
"kafka/#using-the-kafka-connector[SmallRye Reactive Messaging - Kafka "
"Connector Documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each channel can be disabled via configuration using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The most important attributes are listed in the tables below:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Incoming channel configuration (polling from Kafka)"
msgstr ""

msgid "The following attributes are configured using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Some properties have aliases which can be configured globally:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also pass any property supported by the underlying https://kafka."
"apache.org/documentation/#consumerconfigs[Kafka consumer]."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, to configure the `max.poll.records` property, use:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some consumer client properties are configured to sensible default values:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If not set, `reconnect.backoff.max.ms` is set to `10000` to avoid high load "
"on disconnection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If not set, `key.deserializer` is set to `org.apache.kafka.common."
"serialization.StringDeserializer`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The consumer `client.id` is configured according to the number of clients to "
"create using `mp.messaging.incoming.[channel].partitions` property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a `client.id` is provided, it is used as-is or suffixed with client index "
"if `partitions` property is set."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a `client.id` is not provided, it is generated as `kafka-consumer-"
"[channel][-index]`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Incoming Attributes of the 'smallrye-kafka' connector"
msgstr ""

msgid "Attribute (_alias_)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mandatory"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[.no-hyphens]#*bootstrap.servers*#\n"
"\n"
"[.no-hyphens]#_(kafka.bootstrap.servers)_#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of host:port to use for establishing the initial "
"connection to the Kafka cluster.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "false"
msgstr ""

msgid "`localhost:9092`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*topic*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The consumed / populated Kafka topic. If neither this property nor the "
"`topics` properties are set, the channel name is used\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-enabled*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether health reporting is enabled (default) or disabled\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`true`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-readiness-enabled*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether readiness health reporting is enabled (default) or disabled\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-readiness-topic-verification*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"_deprecated_ - Whether the readiness check should verify that topics exist "
"on the broker. Default to false. Enabling it requires an admin connection. "
"Deprecated: Use 'health-topic-verification-enabled' instead.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-readiness-timeout*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"_deprecated_ - During the readiness health check, the connector connects to "
"the broker and retrieves the list of topics. This attribute specifies the "
"maximum duration (in ms) for the retrieval. If exceeded, the channel is "
"considered not-ready. Deprecated: Use 'health-topic-verification-timeout' "
"instead.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _long_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-topic-verification-enabled*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether the startup and readiness check should verify that topics exist on "
"the broker. Default to false. Enabling it requires an admin client "
"connection.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`false`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*health-topic-verification-timeout*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"During the startup and readiness health check, the connector connects to the "
"broker and retrieves the list of topics. This attribute specifies the "
"maximum duration (in ms) for the retrieval. If exceeded, the channel is "
"considered not-ready.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _long_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`2000`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*tracing-enabled*#"
msgstr ""

msgid "Whether tracing is enabled (default) or disabled\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*cloud-events*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Enables (default) or disables the Cloud Event support. If enabled on an "
"_incoming_ channel, the connector analyzes the incoming records and try to "
"create Cloud Event metadata. If enabled on an _outgoing_, the connector "
"sends the outgoing messages as Cloud Event if the message includes Cloud "
"Event Metadata.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*kafka-configuration*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Identifier of a CDI bean that provides the default Kafka consumer/producer "
"configuration for this channel. The channel configuration can still override "
"any attribute. The bean must have a type of Map<String, Object> and must use "
"the @io.smallrye.common.annotation.Identifier qualifier to set the "
"identifier.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*topics*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A comma-separating list of topics to be consumed. Cannot be used with the "
"`topic` or `pattern` properties\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*pattern*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Indicate that the `topic` property is a regular expression. Must be used "
"with the `topic` property. Cannot be used with the `topics` property\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*key.deserializer*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The deserializer classname used to deserialize the record's key\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*value.deserializer*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The deserializer classname used to deserialize the record's value\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "true"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*fetch.min.bytes*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The minimum amount of data the server should return for a fetch request. The "
"default setting of 1 byte means that fetch requests are answered as soon as "
"a single byte of data is available or the fetch request times out waiting "
"for data to arrive.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`1`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*group.id*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A unique string that identifies the consumer group the application belongs "
"to.\n"
"\n"
"If not set, defaults to the application name as set by the `quarkus."
"application.name` configuration property.\n"
"\n"
"If that is not set either, a unique, generated id is used.\n"
"\n"
"It is recommended to always define a `group.id`, the automatic generation is "
"only a convenient feature for development.\n"
"You can explicitly ask for automatically generated unique id by setting this "
"property to `${quarkus.uuid}`.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*enable.auto.commit*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If enabled, consumer's offset will be periodically committed in the "
"background by the underlying Kafka client, ignoring the actual processing "
"outcome of the records. It is recommended to NOT enable this setting and let "
"Reactive Messaging handles the commit.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*retry*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether the connection to the broker is re-attempted in case of failure\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*retry-attempts*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The maximum number of reconnection before failing. -1 means infinite retry\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`-1`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*retry-max-wait*#"
msgstr ""

msgid "The max delay (in seconds) between 2 reconnects\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`30`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*broadcast*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether the Kafka records should be dispatched to multiple consumer\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*auto.offset.reset*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What to do when there is no initial offset in Kafka.Accepted values are "
"earliest, latest and none\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`latest`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*failure-strategy*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify the failure strategy to apply when a message produced from a record "
"is acknowledged negatively (nack). Values can be `fail` (default), `ignore`, "
"or `dead-letter-queue`\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`fail`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*commit-strategy*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify the commit strategy to apply when a message produced from a record "
"is acknowledged. Values can be `latest`, `ignore` or `throttled`. If `enable."
"auto.commit` is true then the default is `ignore` otherwise it is "
"`throttled`\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*throttled.unprocessed-record-max-age.ms*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While using the `throttled` commit-strategy, specify the max age in "
"milliseconds that an unprocessed message can be before the connector is "
"marked as unhealthy. Setting this attribute to 0 disables this monitoring.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`60000`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*dead-letter-queue.topic*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `failure-strategy` is set to `dead-letter-queue` indicates on which "
"topic the record is sent. Defaults is `dead-letter-topic-$channel`\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*dead-letter-queue.key.serializer*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `failure-strategy` is set to `dead-letter-queue` indicates the key "
"serializer to use. If not set the serializer associated to the key "
"deserializer is used\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*dead-letter-queue.value.serializer*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `failure-strategy` is set to `dead-letter-queue` indicates the "
"value serializer to use. If not set the serializer associated to the value "
"deserializer is used\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*partitions*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The number of partitions to be consumed concurrently. The connector creates "
"the specified amount of Kafka consumers. It should match the number of "
"partition of the targeted topic\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*requests*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When `partitions` is greater than 1, this attribute allows configuring how "
"many records are requested by each consumer every time.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`128`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*consumer-rebalance-listener.name*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The name set in `@Identifier` of a bean that implements `io.smallrye."
"reactive.messaging.kafka.KafkaConsumerRebalanceListener`. If set, this "
"rebalance listener is applied to the consumer.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*key-deserialization-failure-handler*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The name set in `@Identifier` of a bean that implements `io.smallrye."
"reactive.messaging.kafka.DeserializationFailureHandler`. If set, "
"deserialization failure happening when deserializing keys are delegated to "
"this handler which may retry or provide a fallback value.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*value-deserialization-failure-handler*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The name set in `@Identifier` of a bean that implements `io.smallrye."
"reactive.messaging.kafka.DeserializationFailureHandler`. If set, "
"deserialization failure happening when deserializing values are delegated to "
"this handler which may retry or provide a fallback value.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*fail-on-deserialization-failure*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When no deserialization failure handler is set and a deserialization failure "
"happens, report the failure and mark the application as unhealthy. If set to "
"`false` and a deserialization failure happens, a `null` value is forwarded.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*graceful-shutdown*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether a graceful shutdown should be attempted when the application "
"terminates.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*poll-timeout*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The polling timeout in milliseconds. When polling records, the poll will "
"wait at most that duration before returning records. Default is 1000ms\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`1000`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*pause-if-no-requests*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether the polling must be paused when the application does not request "
"items and resume when it does. This allows implementing back-pressure based "
"on the application capacity. Note that polling is not stopped, but will not "
"retrieve any records when paused.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*batch*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether the Kafka records are consumed in batch. The channel injection point "
"must consume a compatible type, such as `List<Payload>` or "
"`KafkaRecordBatch<Payload>`.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _boolean_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*max-queue-size-factor*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Multiplier factor to determine maximum number of records queued for "
"processing, using `max.poll.records` * `max-queue-size-factor`. Defaults to "
"2. In `batch` mode `max.poll.records` is considered `1`.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`2`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Outgoing channel configuration (writing to Kafka)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also pass any property supported by the underlying https://kafka."
"apache.org/documentation/#producerconfigs[Kafka producer]."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, to configure the `max.block.ms` property, use:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some producer client properties are configured to sensible default values:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If not set, `key.serializer` is set to `org.apache.kafka.common."
"serialization.StringSerializer`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If not set, producer `client.id` is generated as `kafka-producer-[channel]`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Outgoing Attributes of the 'smallrye-kafka' connector"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*acks*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The number of acknowledgments the producer requires the leader to have "
"received before considering a request complete. This controls the durability "
"of records that are sent. Accepted values are: 0, 1, all\n"
"\n"
"Type: _string_"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*buffer.memory*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The total bytes of memory the producer can use to buffer records waiting to "
"be sent to the server.\n"
"\n"
"Type: _long_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`33554432`"
msgstr ""

msgid "[.no-hyphens]#*close-timeout*#"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The amount of milliseconds waiting for a graceful shutdown of the Kafka "
"producer\n"
"\n"
"Type: _int_"
msgstr ""

msgid "`10000`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[.no-hyphens]#*cloud-events-data-content-type*#\n"
